%I A398172 #32 Sep 15 2026 09:07:12
%S A398172 2,16,230,4812,109536,3599697,101612896,4113975079
%N A398172 Number of subsets of the n X n grid with no three collinear points (the empty set is counted).
%C A398172 a(n) is the number of faces (the empty face included) of the independence complex of the 3-uniform hypergraph whose hyperedges are the collinear triples of the n X n grid (there are A000938(n) such triples). The largest faces have 2n points.
%C A398172 Subsets are counted as sets of grid points; rotations and reflections are counted separately, as in A000755.
%H A398172 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="/A398172/a398172.txt">Two independent programs (Python) for A398172 and A398184</a>
%e A398172 For n = 2 every subset of the 2 X 2 grid is admissible, so a(2) = 2^4 = 16. For n = 3, of the 512 subsets exactly 282 contain one of the 8 collinear triples, so a(3) = 230.
%Y A398172 Row sums of A398580.
%Y A398172 Cf. A398184 (maximal subsets), A000755, A000769, A000938, A277433, A219760.
%K A398172 nonn,more,new
%O A398172 1,1
%A A398172 _Aleksei Kudriashov_, Sep 03 2026
